    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-211995",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14),$ construct a statement that also must be true:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}a≡{{field-2}}b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14)\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nSince the modulus is unchanged in both statements, let's multiply by $3$ and apply the first property.\n\n$$\na≡b\\,⟹\\,3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14)\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
